WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.660
How do you see the shape of a large protein?

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.780
X-ray crystallography needs well-ordered crystals.

3
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.520
NMR in solution works only for relatively small proteins.

4
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.560
Membrane proteins pulled out of the membrane tend to clump.

5
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.420
Electron microscopy had three obstacles.

6
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.620
The beam burns biological material.

7
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.440
A weaker beam gives low contrast.

8
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.120
And the vacuum dries out water-soluble molecules.

9
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:39.033
Purify the molecule, because averaging assumes identical particles.

10
00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:46.133
Spread a small drop as a thin film on a fine metal mesh grid, blot it, and plunge it

11
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.293
into liquid ethane.

12
00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:52.173
Cooling this fast turns the water into glass, not crystals.

13
00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:57.933
A glass is disordered, so the beam scatters evenly and the background is uniform.

14
00:00:58.873 --> 00:01:02.293
The molecules stay in water, not dried or stained.

15
00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.993
Image the frozen grid.

16
00:01:05.813 --> 00:01:12.113
The particles lie in many random orientations, so each image is a flat projection of

17
00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:18.613
a different view. Contrast is very low, so images are taken out of focus, and the

18
00:01:18.613 --> 00:01:22.333
contrast transfer function is measured per image and corrected.

19
00:01:23.753 --> 00:01:25.293
Radiation damage limits the dose.

20
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:33.017
Software picks the particle images, aligns them, and sorts similar views into 2D

21
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:37.637
classes. Averaging a class gives a sharper picture of one view.

22
00:01:38.477 --> 00:01:44.497
Then work out how the views relate in 3D, build a starting model, and refine it

23
00:01:44.497 --> 00:01:45.857
against the particle images.

24
00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:52.097
If the data hold more than one shape, sort the particles into separate 3D classes.

25
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.330
The raw micrograph shows each particle as a faint, noisy shape against grey ice.

26
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:06.770
A class average sums many aligned images of one view, so noise falls and features

27
00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:13.550
appear. The final output is a 3D map with a stated resolution, estimated by

28
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:17.610
splitting the data in two and measuring how well the halves agree.

29
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:22.490
The reported resolution is a broad guideline, not a firm number.

30
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:28.823
Overfitting: aligning noise can create features and inflate the resolution.

31
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:33.083
The control is to refine halves of the data independently.

32
00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:39.783
In one tomography survey, about 90 percent of particles stuck to an air-water interface.

33
00:02:40.323 --> 00:02:45.563
That can denature protein and cause preferred orientations, which means too few

34
00:02:45.563 --> 00:02:52.263
views. Thicker ice, a little detergent, or a thin support film can help, but thicker

35
00:02:52.263 --> 00:02:54.943
ice and most support films cost contrast.

36
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:59.423
Mouse Piezo1 is a membrane protein.

37
00:03:00.403 --> 00:03:08.023
In 2017, Guo and MacKinnon showed the closed trimer at 3.7 Å as a curved,

38
00:03:08.223 --> 00:03:09.483
three-bladed propeller.

39
00:03:10.303 --> 00:03:12.963
In detergent, the micelle forms a dome.

40
00:03:13.923 --> 00:03:19.423
They proposed that in a membrane, tension changes gating energetics in proportion to

41
00:03:19.423 --> 00:03:22.043
the change in projected area under the dome.

42
00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:31.457
In 2022, Jeong, Clark, Gouaux and colleagues solved the native C. elegans TMC-1

43
00:03:31.457 --> 00:03:34.017
complex, a worm structure, not mammalian.

44
00:03:34.837 --> 00:03:42.817
It holds two copies each of TMC-1, CALM-1 and TMIE, and a subset also carried

45
00:03:42.817 --> 00:03:49.317
ARRD-6. Particles from a native extract could be sorted by computer into complexes

46
00:03:49.317 --> 00:03:50.677
with and without it.

47
00:03:51.357 --> 00:03:54.877
A structure is a static reconstruction of purified protein.

48
00:03:55.397 --> 00:03:57.997
It is not a time course or a recording of function.

49
00:03:58.857 --> 00:04:01.177
Pair it with electrophysiology or mutants.
